WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:06.740
This is chapter four of Learn
Text.js: Input and Keymaps.

2
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.810
First, how a key press reaches your app.

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.410
While the page has focus,

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.620
keys land in a hidden textarea
that Text.js adds to the page.

5
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.770
Text.js turns each one into a KeyEvent,
with a normalized key name like up,

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.260
return or escape, the
typed character in input,

7
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.650
and the ctrl, alt, shift and meta flags.

8
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.890
useInput, the low-level hook
you've used so far, receives it.

9
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.770
Call e.stopPropagation to keep the
key from reaching other handlers.

10
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.180
Keys typed into the DevTools prompt go
to DevTools, so click the page first.

11
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.740
Next, keymaps.

12
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.490
Once a screen has more than a couple
of keys, describe them with useKeymap.

13
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.730
Create app/deployments/page.tsx.

14
00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.530
DEPLOYMENTS is a plain array
in lib/deployments.ts for now.

15
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.330
Chapter six moves it
behind a route handler.

16
00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.010
Keep the selected index, and
whether the details are open.

17
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.810
move keeps the index inside the list.

18
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.650
Bindings are strings.

19
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.370
"up, k" means either key.

20
00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.450
enter toggles the details.

21
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.370
And "g g" is a sequence: g, then g again.

22
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.010
A chord like ctrl+k works too.

23
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.250
Every binding here has a label, and
labeled bindings show up in KeyHelp,

24
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.330
KeyHints and the command palette.

25
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:37.420
The selected row gets the selection
background, and KeyHelp goes at the end.

26
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.740
Let's try it, with the help overlay.

27
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.690
Here's the list, live on the lesson page.

28
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.210
Click the pad first.

29
00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.530
Press down, and down again.

30
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.970
j works too.

31
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.890
Enter opens the details.

32
00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.650
Now press the question mark.

33
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.570
KeyHelp lists every labeled
binding that's live right now.

34
00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.170
Press down while it's open, and
the list underneath doesn't move.

35
00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.890
Bindings inside a modal trap focus.

36
00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.610
Press question mark or q to close it.

37
00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.460
Finally, g g jumps back
to the first deployment.

38
00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.500
Last, focus.

39
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:25.570
Components like Input, Select and Table
only take keys while they're focused.

40
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.250
Here the input has focus,
so typing goes into it.

41
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.970
Tab moves focus to the Select, and
now the arrow keys move its highlight.

42
00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:39.540
To move focus yourself, use
useFocus and useFocusManager.

43
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.250
Quick check.

44
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.020
In useKeymap, what does
the binding "g g" mean?

45
00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.850
g, then g again.

46
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.580
Space-separated strokes are a sequence,
and commas separate alternatives.

47
00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.980
Why do you click the page before typing?

48
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:06.170
Keys typed into the DevTools
prompt never reach the page.

49
00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.900
Keystrokes arrive through a hidden input
on the page, so the page needs focus.

50
00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:18.370
Next, in chapter five, you'll split the
app into routes with a shared layout,

51
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.090
and add links with shortcuts and history.

52
00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.740
See you there.
